  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable development programme for landless farmers, bonded labourers &amp; those impacted by mining</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is being undertaken by CPT Marab&#xE1;, CPT Xinguara and CPT Tucuru&#xED;.
CPT in the south of Par&#xE1; state was set up in 1976 as there were deep concerns with the extreme violence and injustice against poor landless farmers. It is a region notorious for violence and impunity with regard to large land owners. CAFOD have been working with CPT since the 1980s. 
This proposal is a development of CPT Xinguara (formally BRA427) and CPT Maraba&#x2019;s (formally BRA404) work to date. The two CPT organisations will now work together under the one project, and will work with the staff of CPT Tucurui in the implementation of this project.
The goal of this project is to contribute to the improvement of living conditions of poor families that live in rural occupations, through accompaniment and legal support to families seeking to realise their right to land and the financial benefits to which they are entitled, that are a result of agrarian reform. The project will also support workers that are experiencing slave labour conditions and/or exploitation, and families and communities that are negatively affected by the impacts of mining expansion in the region. They intend to do this through direct accompaniment and support to those affected, as well as increasing the participation of families, communities and civil society in policy and public programmes at the local, state and federal level, with a view to assuring sustainable socio-environmental development in the south, south-east and Tocantins regions in the State of Par&#xE1;.</narrative>
  </description>
